  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only two experiments are complete. RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 0.485 accuracy while image (resnet50, singleprofile) is very weak at 0.208, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether aggregating multiple profiles per cell (multiprofile) provides meaningful additional signal over a single profile, and this is a foundational design choice that gates many downstream experiments (all multiprofile and multimodal configurations). What this tests: config_002 changes exactly one variable from config_001—switching from singleprofile to multiprofile with the simplest aggregation (avgpool)—while keeping the same PCA encoder. This gives a clean single-variable comparison. Why it is the best next experiment: With only 2 data points, reducing uncertainty about the profile-setting axis is critical. If multiprofile+avgpool improves over 0.485, it validates the multiprofile pathway and justifies investing in multiprofile variants with stronger encoders and multimodal fusion. If it does not improve, we avoid wasting budget on the entire multiprofile sub-grid. The minimal change (one variable) makes the result interpretable, and avgpool as the simplest aggregation isolates the profile-count effect from aggregation-complexity effects."
}

